vaccinating our hospitality workers  governor sysolak held a news conference  today to talk on the efforts to  protect those who are on working on the  front lines here in las vegas and across  the state  sasha loftis joins us from the las vegas  strip with more on the governor's  message  governor select says his goal here is to  make all of southern nevada safer and he  says  that starts with hospitality workers  here on the las vegas strip and really  all across our community  whom he calls the backbone of our  economy the governor joined the chair of  the gaming control board  and other state industry leaders here at  the mandalay bay convention center  the governor says the site has  administered at least 5  000 shots so far and gaming leaders  believe at least  100 000 industry workers have been  reached all across the state  now governor sessalak also spoke about  how these efforts  are helping our economy come back people  ask me when will nevada be back  or what when will vegas be back to all  those who ask  the comeback is here now we are on our  way back  and we are on our way back stronger and  safer  and healthier than ever brynn gibson the  chair of the nevada gaming control board  says some of our state's  largest gaming operators are reporting  60  to 70 percent vaccination rates among  their employees  now governor sisilak thanked everyone  who has gotten vaccinated but  he says our work here isn't done he's  asking anyone who has gotten those shots  to really encourage their friends their  family members their poll workers to get  vaccinated as well  so we can reach herd immunity here  locally faster  reporting from the las vegas strip  tonight sasha loftis 8 news now
 

